Team,

I reviewed the QA note and agree this was misclassified at intake. The transa=
ction is an outgoing wire, so it should have been routed outside the Reg E qu=
eue and handled under the wire process. The customer=E2=80=99s filing path in=
 ClaimTrack needs to be corrected, and the closure letter should not referenc=
e EFT error resolution rights.

Wire transfers made through Fedwire or a similar wire transfer system are not=
 electronic fund transfers under Regulation E and are handled under the Wire =
Transfer Agreement, not this procedure.

Please update the case notes to reflect the reclassification, move the file t=
o the proper disposition queue, and make sure the customer-facing language al=
igns to TERMS-WIRE. Also, QA will log this under DOP-227 as a training opport=
unity for intake. Tasha, please confirm whether the associate followed the in=
take script or if the error occurred when the claim was re-keyed from the con=
tact center referral.

Ifeoma

